THE PREDICTION BEING CHECKED
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  mass_bound (prereg, locked, exact):  |cell(r,d)| <= S(r,d),
  S(r,d) = sum_k C(d,k) N(r-k).  A cell is a signed integer in
  [-S, S].  If cell values were spread over that range, the
  chance of landing exactly on 0 would go like 1/S, giving a
  parameter-free prediction with no free constant:

      density x mean(S)   constant across bases
      density  =  mean(1/S)                 [the sharper form]

  The premise is checked too, at the |cell|/S distribution.

